131
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:46,800
For example, how about a hug from your child?

132
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,960
How much would you have paid for that hug?

133
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:50,480
I wouldn't pay anything for the hug.

134
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:52,640
If I had to pay for it, that would ruin the whole thing.

135
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:56,680
It's got to come for free from the heart in exchange for nothing.

136
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:59,080
Otherwise, it wouldn't make me happy at all.

137
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:01,200
And then, but you do get, oh, wow, that's great.

138
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:03,640
I get the hug from the child, and I love you, Daddy.

139
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:06,000
You're the best daddy in the world.

140
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,880
And that, for many people, they will say, and it seems plausible,

141
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:11,360
that was the best thing that happened to them the entire day,

142
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:13,760
and they wouldn't have paid anything for it.

143
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:18,000
So, that would also seem to be a counter example.

144
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:18,520
All right.

145
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:24,720
Now, the philosophy of utilitarianism, which historically has very close ties to economics.

